␀␀␀FATAL: fb alloc␀FATAL: ST7701 DSI bring-up␀␀RAM ALLOC FAILED␀␀␀␀/ADF/SAMPLE␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.adf␀␀This placeholder shows WHERE your disk image goes.
A real game is an .adf disk image (usually 880KB for Amiga).
The browser ignores any folder named SAMPLE - copy the layout,
don't play in here.
␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.nfo␀␀Title: Sample Game Name
Blurb: 1991 - Publisher Name - one line about the game

This folder is an EXAMPLE ONLY - the browser ignores any folder
named SAMPLE. Copy this layout for real games:

  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.adf   the disk image
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.jpg   cover art (JPEG or PNG, any size)
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.nfo   this info file (plain text)
  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.rtfm  how-to-play manual (plain text, optional)

NFO rules:
  'Title:' overrides the display name (any case: TITLE:/title:).
  'Blurb:' or 'Description:' = info text shown on the cover panel.
  Or skip the labels: first line = title, following lines = blurb.

Multi-disk games: YourGame-1.adf, YourGame-2.adf, ...
Same pattern applies in /DSK for .dsk images.
␀␀␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.jpg␀␀/ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.rtfm␀HOW TO PLAY - and how this MANUAL works
=======================================

You are reading the GTi manual viewer. This text came
from a plain-text file sitting next to the game:

  /ADF/SAMPLE/Sample.rtfm

Any game can have one. Drop a file named the same as
the disk, ending in .rtfm, beside it:

  /ADF/YourGame/YourGame.rtfm

...and a little book button appears on the cover art.
Tap it to read the game's instructions - controls,
cheats, copy-protection answers, whatever you like.

USING THE READER
  - Drag up or down to scroll; flick for a fast spin.
  - SIZE cycles SMALL / NORMAL / LARGE text, following
    your menu font setting.
  - CLOSE (or tap the page) returns to the library.

TIPS
  - Keep it plain ASCII text. Accents and smart quotes
    are cleaned up for you, but plain is safest.
  - Blank lines make paragraphs. Short lines read best.
  - Manuals are meant to be short and handy - a page or
    two of how-to-play basics.

Read the fine manual. :)

- OMEGAWARE
␀␀␀␀# Gotek Touchscreen Interface - OMEGAWARE␀␀␀# Edit values below, then reboot.␀␀␀# Theme: 0=NAVY 1=EMBER 2=MATRIX 3=PAPER 4=SYNTH 5=GOLD␀THEME=0␀# Transfer mode: STANDALONE (USB to Gotek) or WIRELESS (ESP-NOW to dongle)␀␀MODE=STANDALONE␀# CAROUSEL: default boot view. OFF=game list, ON=cover reel, LAST=restore last view.␀␀␀␀CAROUSEL=OFF␀␀␀␀# Loop cracktro splash: 1=loop until tapped, 0=auto-dismiss after 6s␀␀␀␀LOOP=0␀␀# Boot cracktro style: 0=random each boot, or pick one:␀#   1=COPPER CLASSIC  2=STARFIELD  3=RAINBOW RASTER␀#   4=PLASMA  5=BOING BALL  6=SYNTHWAVE␀CRACKTRO=0␀␀# Font size: SMALL, NORMAL, LARGE␀␀␀FONT=NORMAL␀# Language: EN, FR, IT, ES, DE  (pull the SD and edit this line if you get stuck)␀␀␀LANG=EN␀# Screen rotation in degrees: 0 or 180 = landscape, 90 or 270 = portrait.␀␀␀# Easiest to set with the ROTATE button on the INFO screen (each tap = +90).␀␀␀␀ROTATE=0␀␀␀␀# COMPACT: OFF = cover art + list, ON = maximise the game list (cover collapses to a strip)␀COMPACT=OFF␀# BTNSTYLE: reel button style. PILL=rounded coloured buttons (default), FLAT=flat bar.␀␀BTNSTYLE=PILL␀␀␀# CAP: max wireless dongles the scan will list (default 32, up to 64)␀␀␀CAP=32␀␀# HIVEMIND: wireless FLING fan-out. ON=send to all paired MuCa dongles (classic), OFF=only the selected dongle.␀HIVEMIND=ON␀# Load/eject behaviour (all OFF = safest: select, then press the button)␀␀␀␀# TAPLOAD: ON = tapping the already-highlighted game row loads it (old double-tap)␀␀TAPLOAD=OFF␀# HOTSWAP: ON = tapping another disk while loaded swaps to it instantly␀HOTSWAP=OFF␀# FORCESWAP: ON = swap disk contents without the USB eject/re-attach cycle␀␀FORCESWAP=OFF␀␀␀# SAVES: save-game persistence when the Amiga writes to the disk.␀␀␀#   OFF       = writes live only until eject/power-off (classic behaviour)␀␀#   COPY      = writes are kept as GameName.sav.adf beside the master (recommended)␀#   OVERWRITE = writes are patched straight into the master .adf␀␀␀␀SAVES=COPY␀␀# SDSPEED: SD card clock speed.␀#   20 = safe default, works with every card.␀␀␀#   40 = ~1.7x faster reads if your card can hold it (auto-falls back to 20 if it can't mount).␀SDSPEED=20␀␀# CATEGORIES: OFF = one flat library (classic). ON = browse by category â€”␀#   any top-level folder that holds NO disk images (only subfolders) becomes a category.␀␀␀␀CATEGORIES=OFF␀␀# NESTING: OFF = categories are one level deep. ON = allow sub-categories (folders within category folders).␀␀␀␀NESTING=OFF␀# SCREENSAVER: idle slideshow. ON = show it after a few minutes idle, OFF = never.␀␀SCREENSAVER=ON␀␀# SSMODE: SLIDES = full-screen photo slideshow (default), BOUNCE = bouncing logo, MATRIX = code rain.␀␀␀SSMODE=SLIDES␀␀␀# SSFX: transition between slides - SHUFFLE (random), FADE, DISSOLVE, SLIDE, or CUT.␀␀␀␀SSFX=SHUFFLE␀␀␀␀# SSTIME: seconds each slide is shown (2-120).␀␀SSTIME=6␀␀␀␀# SSFAV: ON = also slideshow the cover art of your favourited games;␀␀␀␀#        OFF = only images you drop in the /screensaver/ folder.␀␀␀␀SSFAV=ON␀␀␀␀# LINK: dongle transport. ESPNOW = the dongle's own AP + ESP-NOW (default).␀#       HOMEWIFI = route the FLING via your home router to a Webby dongle's gotek.local.␀␀␀␀LINK=ESPNOW␀# HOME_SSID / HOME_PASS: your home WiFi (only used when LINK=HOMEWIFI).␀HOME_SSID=␀␀HOME_PASS=␀␀# DONGLE_HOME_IP: auto-filled cache of the dongle's home IP (mDNS gotek.local is primary).␀␀DONGLE_HOME_IP=␀# Wireless dongle MAC (auto-filled when you pair via INFO screen)␀␀␀# XIAO_MAC=␀by Vinay Dhir␀␀␀~ PURPLE DREAMS ~␀␀␀        OMEGAWARE PRESENTS ...  DENISE  ...  BUILT BY VINAY DHIR ...  PURPLE DREAMS ...  GREETINGS FROM THE GTi CREW ...  NOW GO LOAD A GAME ...        ␀␀␀␀@WRANGLER_AMIGA␀A GENUINE GAMECHANGER␀␀␀        BIG RESPECT TO WRANGLER_AMIGA ...  THE MAN WHO SHOWED THE GTi TO THE WORLD ...  A GENUINE GAMECHANGER - HIS WORDS, NOT OURS ...  CHEERS FOR THE COVERAGE, LEGEND ...  FIND HIM ON YOUTUBE @ WRANGLER_AMIGA ...  NOW GO WRANGLE A FLOPPY ...        ␀        OMEGAWARE x RETRONAUT ...  AN EXCLUSIVE FIRST LOOK FOR THE CHANNEL ...  CHEERS FOR THE VIDEO, LEGEND ...  LOGO FLOWN WITH PERMISSION ...  NOW GO LOAD A GAME ...        ␀␀␀␀CRACKED - TRAINED - LOADED␀␀        OMEGAWARE PRESENTS ... THE GTi ... THE FLOPPY FLINGER THINGER ... CODED BY MEZ & DIMMY ... A LITTLE TRIBUTE TO THE AMIGA CRACKTRO LEGENDS ... GREETINGS TO EVERYONE KEEPING THE SCENE ALIVE ... NOW GO LOAD A GAME ...        ␀␀* MEZ & DIMMY *␀INTO THE VOID␀␀␀MELT YOUR EYES␀␀RETRO FUTURE␀␀␀␀TAP TO CONTINUE␀ESP32␀␀␀RAMDISK␀Image: unrecognised (not GTi-JC)␀␀␀␀Image: not a firmware .bin␀␀Image: GTi-JC firmware  [OK]␀␀␀␀FLASH␀␀␀FLASH ANYWAY␀␀␀␀read/write error - image unchanged␀␀.BIN␀␀␀␀JC35␀␀␀␀/GTi_update.bin␀NO UPDATE FILE␀␀Drop a GTi-JC35-*.bin on the SD␀(no rename needed), then try again.␀SD UPDATE NOT ENABLED␀␀␀This unit needs ONE more USB flash␀␀(web flasher) to add the OTA layout.␀␀␀␀After that, SD updates work forever.␀␀␀␀FIRMWARE UPDATE␀File: %u KB␀5.9.3-P4␀␀␀␀Now running: %s␀! flash only a GTi-JC .bin here␀CANCEL␀␀FLASHING - DO NOT UNPLUG␀␀␀␀UPDATE FAILED␀␀␀current firmware kept.␀␀.installed␀␀UPDATE OK - REBOOTING␀␀␀< ..␀␀␀␀NORMAL␀␀(c)␀(r)␀deg␀AAAAAAECEEEEIIIIDNOOOOOxOUUUUYPsaaaaaaeceeeeiiiidnooooo/ouuuuypy␀␀␀␀(no manual text)␀␀␀␀%␀␀␀SIZE:␀␀␀TOP␀SECTIONS␀␀␀␀JUMP TO SECTION␀Vincent␀@wrangler_amiga␀DEL␀SPACE␀␀␀SAVE␀␀␀␀UNLOCK␀␀LOCKED␀␀UNLOCKED␀␀␀␀Looking for dongles...␀␀BACK␀␀␀␀Dongles (␀␀␀) - pick one:␀␀␀Dongle ␀OMEGA-␀␀USE␀RENAME␀␀PAIRED␀␀REMOVED␀/USER-DISKS/USER%02d.adf␀␀␀␀USER%02d␀␀␀␀RENAME DISK␀ESPNOW␀␀PILL␀␀␀␀ match␀␀ matches␀␀␀␀ENTERING SD ACCESS...␀␀␀SLIDES␀␀type to find a game␀1234567890␀␀QWERTYUIOP␀␀ASDFGHJKL-␀␀ZXCVBNM'.␀␀␀BlindGuy␀␀␀␀Retronaut␀␀␀Mez␀Wrangler␀␀␀␀
# Theme: 0=NAVY 1=EMBER 2=MATRIX 3=PAPER 4=SYNTH 5=GOLD
THEME=0
␀␀␀
# Transfer mode: STANDALONE (USB to Gotek) or WIRELESS (ESP-NOW to dongle)
MODE=STANDALONE
␀␀␀␀
# CAROUSEL: default boot view. OFF=game list, ON=cover reel, LAST=restore last view.
CAROUSEL=OFF
␀
# Loop cracktro splash: 1=loop until tapped, 0=auto-dismiss after 6s
LOOP=0
␀␀␀
# Boot cracktro style: 0=random each boot, or pick one:
#   1=COPPER CLASSIC  2=STARFIELD  3=RAINBOW RASTER
#   4=PLASMA  5=BOING BALL  6=SYNTHWAVE
CRACKTRO=0
␀␀␀␀
# Font size: SMALL, NORMAL, LARGE
FONT=NORMAL
␀
# Language: EN, FR, IT, ES, DE  (pull the SD and edit this line if you get stuck)
LANG=EN
␀
# Screen rotation in degrees: 0 or 180 = landscape, 90 or 270 = portrait.
ROTATE=0
␀␀␀␀
# COVERMIN: hide covers whose short side is under N px (0 = show all) - keeps the reel + panel clean.
COVERMIN=140
␀␀␀␀
# REELFILTER: ON = the reel (cover carousel) shows only games whose cover passes COVERMIN;
#             the A-Z list still shows every game. OFF = reel shows all games.
REELFILTER=OFF
␀␀
# COMPACT: OFF = cover art + list, ON = maximise the game list (cover collapses to a strip)
COMPACT=OFF
␀␀␀
# BTNSTYLE: reel button style. PILL=rounded coloured buttons (default), FLAT=flat bar.
BTNSTYLE=PILL
␀␀
# CAP: max wireless dongles the scan will list (default 32, up to 64)
CAP=32
␀␀
# HIVEMIND: wireless FLING fan-out. ON=all paired MuCa dongles (classic), OFF=selected dongle only.
HIVEMIND=ON
␀␀␀
# TAPLOAD: ON = tapping the already-highlighted game row loads it (old double-tap)
TAPLOAD=OFF
␀␀␀␀# HOTSWAP: ON = tapping another disk while loaded swaps to it instantly
HOTSWAP=OFF
␀␀␀␀# FORCESWAP: ON = swap disk contents without the USB eject/re-attach cycle
FORCESWAP=OFF
␀␀␀
# SAVES: save-game persistence. OFF = classic (lost on eject),
# COPY = kept as GameName.sav.adf beside the master, OVERWRITE = patch the master.
SAVES=COPY
␀␀
# SDSPEED: SD card clock. 20 = safe default, 40 = ~1.7x faster reads if your card holds it (auto-falls back to 20).
SDSPEED=20
␀␀␀␀
# CATEGORIES: OFF = flat library. ON = browse by category (a top-level folder with no disk images, only subfolders, is a category).
CATEGORIES=OFF
␀␀␀␀# NESTING: OFF = one category level. ON = allow sub-categories (folders within category folders).
NESTING=OFF
␀␀
# SCREENSAVER: idle slideshow. ON = show it after a few minutes idle, OFF = never.
SCREENSAVER=ON
␀# SSMODE: SLIDES = full-screen photo slideshow (default), BOUNCE = bouncing logo, MATRIX = code rain.
SSMODE=SLIDES
␀␀␀␀# SSFX: transition between slides - SHUFFLE (random), FADE, DISSOLVE, SLIDE, or CUT.
SSFX=SHUFFLE
␀␀# SSTIME: seconds each slide is shown (2-120).
SSTIME=6
␀␀␀␀# SSFAV: ON = also slideshow favourited game covers; OFF = only /screensaver/ images.
SSFAV=ON
␀
# LINK: dongle transport. ESPNOW = the dongle's own AP + ESP-NOW (default). HOMEWIFI = route the FLING via your home router to a Webby dongle's gotek.local.
LINK=ESPNOW
␀␀# HOME_SSID: your home WiFi name (only used when LINK=HOMEWIFI).
HOME_SSID=
␀␀␀␀# HOME_PASS: your home WiFi password (only used when LINK=HOMEWIFI).
HOME_PASS=
␀␀␀␀# DONGLE_HOME_IP: auto-filled cache of the dongle's home-network IP (mDNS gotek.local is the primary lookup).
